        "original_id": "8172b24a-5829-5ebf-afd4-9da669c02717",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Teams: Sacramento Kings, Phoenix Suns\n- People: Bobby Hurley, Wayman Tisdale\n- Organizations: National Basketball Association, Duke University\n- Events: 1993–94 NBA season, 1993 NBA draft\n\nFacts:\n- The 1993–94 NBA season was the Sacramento Kings' 45th season in the National Basketball Association and their ninth season in Sacramento.\n- In the 1993 NBA draft, the Sacramento Kings selected Bobby Hurley from Duke University as their top draft pick.\n- Entering the 1993–94 season, the Sacramento Kings won three of their first four games.\n- Early in the 1993–94 season, the Sacramento Kings then lost 12 of their next 13 games, including an eight-game losing streak.\n- After the 1993–94 season, Wayman Tisdale signed with the Phoenix Suns as a free agent.\n- Wayman Tisdale, born on June 9, 1964, was an American NBA player and a smooth jazz bass guitarist.\n- Wayman Tisdale died on May 15, 2009.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b57309be-fc3a-5727-9966-09ab36704e98",
        "text": "Page: 1993–94 Sacramento Kings season. Sentence: The 1993–94 NBA season was the Kings' 45th season in the National Basketball Association, and ninth season in Sacramento.\nPage: 1993–94 Sacramento Kings season. Sentence: With top draft pick Bobby Hurley from Duke University in the 1993 NBA draft, the Kings had a renewed optimism entering the season winning three of their first four games.\nPage: 1993–94 Sacramento Kings season. Sentence: However, they proceeded to lose 12 of their next 13 games including eight straight losses.\nPage: 1993–94 Sacramento Kings season. Sentence: Following the season, Wayman Tisdale signed as a free agent with the Phoenix Suns.\nPage: Wayman Tisdale. Sentence: Wayman Lawrence Tisdale (June 9, 1964 – May 15, 2009) was an American professional basketball player in the NBA and a smooth jazz bass guitarist.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
